[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186172101 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e6203f86-9cf0-5174-84bf-8575e36ffa78"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6203f86-9cf0-5174-84bf-8575e36ffa78" :question/id #uuid "e6203f86-9cf0-5174-84bf-8575e36ffa78" :question/math-academy-id "q-127310" :question/problem "Use the flux form of Green's theorem to calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=⟨{e}^{2y}+4x,\\,{x}^{7}-{y}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nthrough the boundary of the square $-1\\le x\\le 0,-1\\le y\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/09/09acd3df62b333bdaeb7553599507d4dbad7412ef2770b00e8fc8855b38a774e.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={e}^{2y}+4x$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{7}-{y}^{2}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the rectangular region $D$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y):-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)[x]_{-1}^{0}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\cdot 1\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\,dy \\\\  & =[4y-{y}^{2}]_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =0-(4(-1)-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64fabadb-f80e-5526-b940-02e3d7342ff0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64fabadb-f80e-5526-b940-02e3d7342ff0" :answer-field/id #uuid "64fabadb-f80e-5526-b940-02e3d7342ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bcf09cf2-93d1-5582-bc68-59720e36e72f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e59702b-e79a-5b04-9309-46a6ac9eac76" "answer-f58d9465-726d-5a95-9c7d-efc84289b65d" "answer-1fa26e4c-314f-5b70-a15a-1830ec32c897" "answer-61157c7e-b646-58f6-a043-51dc356ac96d" "answer-bcf09cf2-93d1-5582-bc68-59720e36e72f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e59702b-e79a-5b04-9309-46a6ac9eac76" :answer/id #uuid "8e59702b-e79a-5b04-9309-46a6ac9eac76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f58d9465-726d-5a95-9c7d-efc84289b65d" :answer/id #uuid "f58d9465-726d-5a95-9c7d-efc84289b65d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fa26e4c-314f-5b70-a15a-1830ec32c897" :answer/id #uuid "1fa26e4c-314f-5b70-a15a-1830ec32c897" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61157c7e-b646-58f6-a043-51dc356ac96d" :answer/id #uuid "61157c7e-b646-58f6-a043-51dc356ac96d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcf09cf2-93d1-5582-bc68-59720e36e72f" :answer/id #uuid "bcf09cf2-93d1-5582-bc68-59720e36e72f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6ad25cf5-915c-59ed-8b39-5e9a6998c5a8" :activity/id #uuid "6ad25cf5-915c-59ed-8b39-5e9a6998c5a8" :activity/title "Green's Theorem in Flux Form" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050694 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-b61a74fa-7b3b-5a75-9b36-4b9533c9a9cd" "step-4