he region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/09/09acd3df62b333bdaeb7553599507d4dbad7412ef2770b00e8fc8855b38a774e.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={e}^{2y}+4x$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{7}-{y}^{2}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the rectangular region $D$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y):-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)[x]_{-1}^{0}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\cdot 1\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\,dy \\\\  & =[4y-{y}^{2}]_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =0-(4(-1)-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-e6203f86-9cf0-5174-84bf-8575e36ffa78" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-64fabadb-f80e-5526-b940-02e3d7342ff0" :answer-field/id #uuid "64fabadb-f80e-5526-b940-02e3d7342ff0"] ["answer-8e59702b-e79a-5b04-9309-46a6ac9eac76" :answer/id #uuid "8e59702b-e79a-5b04-9309-46a6ac9eac76"] ["answer-8e59702b-e79a-5b04-9309-46a6ac9eac76" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8e59702b-e79a-5b04-9309-46a6ac9eac76" :answer/value "-4"] ["answer-f58d9465-726d-5a95-9c7d-efc84289b65d" :answer/id #uuid "f58d9465-726d-5a95-9c7d-efc84289b65d"] ["answer-f58d9465-726d-5a95-9c7d-efc84289b65d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f58d9465-726d-5a95-